{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"82c440d532b032fb","name":"card_event_air_cover_us","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/USA/NavalWarfare/events/card_event_air_cover_us","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"AIR COVER","text":"Add two BREWSTER F2A to the battlefield, in the frontline if possible.","flavorText":"During WWII, the United States deployed a range of fighter aircraft to provide air cover for ground forces, naval convoys, and strategic locations. The Brewster F2A Buffalo, one of the Navy’s first monoplanes, was quickly outclassed by Japanese Zeros due to its poor speed and maneuverability. But despite heavy losses in early battles, it provided adequate defense until replaced by the Grumman F4F Wildcat. The F6F Hellcat was introduced in January 1943, and its superior range, firepower, and survivability helped secure Allied air superiority in the Pacific. The P-38 Lightning operated globally for the USAAF, while the P-47 Thunderbolt and P-51 Mustang dominated in Europe.","faction":"USA","type":"order","rarity":"Common","cost":3,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_air_cover_us","title":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_air_cover_us_title","SourceString":"AIR COVER","LocalizedString":"AIR COVER"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::USA","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_air_cover_us_text","SourceString":"Add two BREWSTER F2A to the battlefield, in the frontline if possible.","LocalizedString":"Add two BREWSTER F2A to the battlefield, in the frontline if possible."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_air_cover_us_history","SourceString":"During WWII, the United States deployed a range of fighter aircraft to provide air cover for ground forces, naval convoys, and strategic locations. The Brewster F2A Buffalo, one of the Navy’s first monoplanes, was quickly outclassed by Japanese Zeros due to its poor speed and maneuverability. But despite heavy losses in early battles, it provided adequate defense until replaced by the Grumman F4F Wildcat. The F6F Hellcat was introduced in January 1943, and its superior range, firepower, and survivability helped secure Allied air superiority in the Pacific. The P-38 Lightning operated globally for the USAAF, while the P-47 Thunderbolt and P-51 Mustang dominated in Europe.","LocalizedString":"During WWII, the United States deployed a range of fighter aircraft to provide air cover for ground forces, naval convoys, and strategic locations. The Brewster F2A Buffalo, one of the Navy’s first monoplanes, was quickly outclassed by Japanese Zeros due to its poor speed and maneuverability. But despite heavy losses in early battles, it provided adequate defense until replaced by the Grumman F4F Wildcat. The F6F Hellcat was introduced in January 1943, and its superior range, firepower, and survivability helped secure Allied air superiority in the Pacific. The P-38 Lightning operated globally for the USAAF, while the P-47 Thunderbolt and P-51 Mustang dominated in Europe."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::NavalWarfare","draftBaseWeight":0.9,"spawnCardName":"card_unit_brewster_f2a","soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'AU_Flyby_Fighter_small_Cue'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Fighters/AU_Flyby_Fighter_small_Cue.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/USA/NavalWarfare/t_air_cover.t_air_cover","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Roy Grinnell","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/AIR_COVER.AIR_COVER","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":384.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_usa","Key":"card_event_air_cover_us_photo","SourceString":"A US P-38 escorting B-17 bombers over Germany. Date unknown.","LocalizedString":"A US P-38 escorting B-17 bombers over Germany. Date unknown."},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_At